Update jcode to 0.97.0

Upstream release.  The NetBSD stdin-detection patchset carried since 0.90.0
still applies, with one change: the `#[cfg(target_os = "linux")]` gate on the
std::process import in crates/jcode-core/src/stdin_detect_tests.rs has landed
upstream, so patch-crates_jcode-core_src_stdin_detect_tests.rs loses that hunk
and now only appends the NetBSD status-line parser tests.

rquickjs-sys 0.14.0 is new in this release and ships no NetBSD bindings, which
breaks the build.  post-extract aliases the equivalent -linux-gnu bindings to
the NetBSD triples; see the comment in the Makefile for why that is correct and
preferable to enabling the crate's bindgen feature.
